{
  "id": "v10_two_merchants_of_record",
  "title": "Two merchants of record in one order: both chains verify",
  "test_plan_vector": "10",
  "spec": [
    "Platform Verification 1: MUST verify each receipt's signature against the `keys` of the business named in `iss`. A receipt whose `typ` is not `ucp-ap2-receipt+jwt`, or whose `kid` does not resolve in the `keys` of `iss`, is `receipt_invalid_signature`.",
    "Platform Verification 4: MUST evaluate `seq` and `prev` continuity per `(iss, mandate_ref)` chain. A byte-identical redelivery of a receipt the platform already holds is ignored. A second, different receipt for a `seq` the platform already holds is `receipt_sequence_gap`; the platform keeps both. A receipt whose `prev` is the hash of a receipt reported as `receipt_sequence_gap` continues the chain from that receipt and is not itself a gap.",
    "Platform Verification 6: MUST check that `authorized` and `captured` do not exceed `mandated` (`receipt_exceeds_mandate`), that `captured` does not exceed `authorized` (`receipt_capture_exceeds_authorization`), and that `refunded` does not exceed `captured` (`receipt_refund_exceeds_capture`). The check uses the recomputed totals, or the stated totals for the receipt at which recomputation stopped and every receipt after it. An outcome is reported on every receipt for which the totals are over, not only the first. These outcomes are independent of `receipt_totals_mismatch`: a receipt can report both.",
    "Edge Cases, Several merchants of record in one Order: each has its own mandate and keys, so each `(iss, mandate_ref)` pair is an independent chain."
  ],
  "signing": "TEST-ONLY P-256 keys derived from fixed labels in common/payments/ap2_receipt_fixtures.py; deterministic ECDSA (RFC 6979). Never use them outside these vectors.",
